.TH LUMEN-SYNC 1 "September 18, 2026" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lumen-sync \- Sync opencode and pi coding-agent configs with the live NCSA Lumen catalog
.SH SYNOPSIS
lumen-sync [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
lumen-sync queries the NCSA Lumen API at \fBhttps://lumen.ncsa.illinois.edu/v1/models\fP and reconciles the Lumen provider configuration in one or both supported coding harnesses:

.RS 4
.IP \(bu 3
opencode: the \fIprovider.lumen.models\fP block in \fI~/.config/opencode/opencode.json\fP
.IP \(bu 3
pi: the \fIproviders.ncsa-lumen.models\fP list in \fI~/.pi/agent/models.json\fP
.RE

It adds real models from the live catalog (with context/cost metadata), removes phantom entries Lumen no longer lists, and leaves everything else (other providers, auth, extensions, settings) untouched.

By default lumen-sync performs a dry-run showing what would change without writing anything. Use \fB--apply\fP to write. Each target file is backed up with a timestamp before writing and restored automatically if the written file fails to re-parse.

Config files are fingerprinted when read. If a file changes between the read and the write (another terminal or agent session editing it, or the harness rewriting its own config), \fB--apply\fP refuses to write and exits without modifying anything; re-run to pick up the new state.

Since version 2.0.0 the default target is \fBboth\fP harnesses. Use \fB--target opencode\fP for the version 1.x behavior.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB--apply\fP
Write changes to the target config files. Timestamped backups are created automatically.
.TP
\fB--target {both,opencode,pi}\fP
Which harness config to sync (default: \fBboth\fP).
.TP
\fB--list\fP
Print the live Lumen catalog with model names, context windows, and pricing, then exit. No changes are made.
.TP
\fB--no-prune\fP
When used with \fB--apply\fP, adds/updates models from Lumen but preserves configured entries that are not present in the Lumen catalog (disables pruning).
.TP
\fB--config \fIPATH\fR
Path to opencode.json (default: \fI~/.config/opencode/opencode.json\fP).
.TP
\fB--provider-key \fIKEY\fR
Provider key inside opencode.json (default: \fBlumen\fP).
.TP
\fB--pi-config \fIPATH\fR
Path to pi models.json (default: \fI~/.pi/agent/models.json\fP).
.TP
\fB--pi-provider \fIKEY\fR
Provider key inside pi models.json (default: \fBncsa-lumen\fP).
.TP
\fB--pi-settings \fIPATH\fR
Path to pi settings.json, checked so the pi default model is updated if it disappears from the catalog (default: \fI~/.pi/agent/settings.json\fP).
.TP
\fB--base-url \fIURL\fR
Lumen API endpoint (default: \fBhttps://lumen.ncsa.illinois.edu/v1\fP).
.TP
\fB-q, --quiet\fP
Suppress non-error output (good for cron).
.TP
\fB--help\fP
Display help message and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBLUMEN_API_KEY\fP
Required. Your NCSA Lumen API key, read from the environment for API calls. Set it in your shell profile (e.g., ~/.zshrc):
    export LUMEN_API_KEY=your_actual_key_here
.SH AUTH NOTES
The tool never modifies opencode's \fIoptions.apiKey\fP (which may be a literal key or a \fB{env:LUMEN_API_KEY}\fP reference).

pi does not support environment-variable references for custom providers, so its \fIapiKey\fP is a literal value in \fImodels.json\fP. The tool preserves any existing key and enforces file mode 600 on every write. If it creates the pi provider fresh (no existing config), it writes the key from \fB$LUMEN_API_KEY\fP, again mode 600.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/opencode/opencode.json\fP
opencode configuration (modified with \fB--apply\fP, target opencode or both).
.TP
\fI~/.pi/agent/models.json\fP
pi provider/model catalog (modified with \fB--apply\fP, target pi or both; always written mode 600).
.TP
\fI~/.pi/agent/settings.json\fP
pi settings; only rewritten if the configured default model vanished from the catalog.
.TP
\fI*.lumen-sync-backup-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS\fP
Timestamped backups created before every write.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Preview changes for both harnesses (dry-run):
    lumen-sync
.PP
Apply to both (automatic timestamped backups):
    lumen-sync --apply
.PP
Only pi:
    lumen-sync --target pi --apply
.PP
Only opencode (version 1.x behavior):
    lumen-sync --target opencode --apply
.PP
View the current Lumen model catalog:
    lumen-sync --list
.PP
Apply but keep entries Lumen no longer lists:
    lumen-sync --apply --no-prune
.SH EXIT STATUS
0   Success.
1   Error (missing API key, network issues, file permissions, or a failed write that was rolled back).
2   Invalid command-line usage.
